  "Question": "If \\(~\\begin{array}{r|l}a&b \\\\ \\hline c&d\\end{array} = a\\cdot d-b\\cdot c,\\) what is the value of \\(~\\begin{array}{r|l}3&4 \\\\ \\hline 1&2\\end{array}~?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2 \\)",
    "B": "\\(-1 \\)",
    "C": "\\(0 \\)",
    "D": "\\(1 \\)",
    "E": "\\(2 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Match each entry with its position in the rule: \\(a=3\\), \\(b=4\\), \\(c=1\\), and \\(d=2\\). Therefore\n\\[\na\\cdot d-b\\cdot c\n=3\\cdot2-4\\cdot1\n=6-4=\\boxed{2}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice E.",
